{% comment %}
  The call-to-action rail that repeats down a long landing page: one button
  back to the buy box, with the reassurance under it.

  Kept in one place so every rail on a page is the same shape — a page that
  asks for the sale six times should not ask for it six different ways.

  Accepts:
  - label: {String} Button text. Nothing renders without it.
  - url: {String} Where it goes. Defaults to the bundle anchor.
  - footnote: {String} Reassurance under the button. One item per line as
      "icon | label" renders each with its icon side by side; anything else is
      printed as a plain line.
  - id: {String} The section id, for the scoped style rule.
  - width: {String} 'auto' (default) sizes the button to its label; 'full'
      stretches it across the column up to a readable maximum, as a landing
      page's primary action.
  - align: {String} 'center' (default), 'left' or 'right'.
  - arrow: {Boolean} Adds an arrow after the label.
  - show: {Boolean|String} Overrides the theme switch that hides every in-page
      rail, for a rail that should appear either way. true or 'always' keeps it;
      false or 'never' drops it. The strings are there because a caller whose
      boolean arrives as text would otherwise be read as "no opinion" and
      silently lose its button.
  - gift: {String} A second line inside the button, for a gift that comes with
      every order. Falls back to the theme setting so one edit changes every
      rail on the page; pass 'none' to leave it off a particular rail.
  - gift_icon: {String} The icon that opens that line. Default 'gift'.
      Inside the text itself, [name] becomes that icon where it stands, so a
      line can read "Get FREE X [bottle] - $49 value".

  Usage:
  {% render 'ces-cta-rail',
     label: section.settings.cta_label,
     url: section.settings.cta_url,
     footnote: section.settings.cta_footnote,
     id: section.id %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    A page can be set to carry its call to action only in the sticky bar. The
    rails then render nothing at all rather than being hidden with CSS, so
    they cost no markup and leave no gap where they used to sit. A single rail
    can still be silenced on its own by clearing its button label.
  endcomment
  comment
    The switch belongs to the product page, because the sticky bar that is
    meant to replace these buttons is a product-template section. Applied
    everywhere it took the call to action off the home page and left nothing
    in its place.
  endcomment
  assign rail_off = false
  if settings.ces_hide_inline_ctas and request.page_type == 'product'
    assign rail_off = true
  endif
  if show == false or show == 'never' or show == 'false'
    assign rail_off = true
  endif
  if show == true or show == 'always' or show == 'true'
    assign rail_off = false
  endif
-%}
{%- if label != blank and rail_off != true -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      The gift is the same on every rail, so it is a theme setting rather than
      a field repeated in fifteen sections. A rail can still opt out.
    endcomment
    assign rail_gift = gift | default: settings.ces_cta_gift
    if gift == 'none'
      assign rail_gift = ''
    endif
    comment
      The opening icon defaults to none because an icon written into the text
      flows and centres with the words; one held outside as a flex item sits
      hard left of a sentence that has wrapped.
    endcomment
    assign rail_gift_icon = gift_icon | default: settings.ces_cta_gift_icon | default: 'none'

    comment
      An icon can also stand inside the sentence, written as [name]. Splitting
      on '[' leaves each later chunk as "name]rest", so the chunk is split
      again on ']' to separate the two.
    endcomment
    assign rail_gift_chunks = rail_gift | split: '['

    assign rail_rows = footnote | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
    assign rail_structured = false
    if footnote contains '|'
      assign rail_structured = true
    endif
  -%}

  {%- style -%}
    .ces-cta-rail{margin:2.8rem 0 0;text-align:center}
    .ces-cta-rail--left{text-align:left}
    .ces-cta-rail--left .ces-cta-rail__trust{justify-content:flex-start}
    .ces-cta-rail--right{text-align:right}
    .ces-cta-rail--right .ces-cta-rail__trust{justify-content:flex-end}
    /* The primary action is the same block wherever it appears, so it is given
       one size rather than taking the width of whatever label it carries.
       Measured off the reference: 440px at most, centred, 65px tall and 60px
       on a phone. */
    .ces-cta-rail--full .ces-cta-rail__box{width:100%;max-width:44rem;margin:0 auto}
    .ces-cta-rail--full .ces-button{display:flex;width:100%;min-height:6rem;
      justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:1rem;text-align:center;font-size:2rem}
    @media screen and (min-width:750px){
      .ces-cta-rail--full .ces-button{min-height:6.5rem;font-size:2.4rem}
    }
    /* With a gift the button carries two lines: the action, then what comes
       with it. Stacked inside the one target rather than printed beneath it,
       so the offer cannot be read as belonging to the next block. */
    /* The gift line must be allowed to wrap. A flex item will not shrink below
       its content, so a nowrap line here set the button's minimum width and
       pushed it past the screen on a phone. */
    /* The icon stays on the line: left to wrap it went above the words and the
       second line of the button read as two. The words shrink instead, which
       needs min-width:0 because a flex item will not go below its content. */
    .ces-cta-rail__gift{display:inline-flex;flex-wrap:nowrap;align-items:center;
      justify-content:center;max-width:100%;min-width:0;
      gap:.6rem;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;opacity:.92;
      letter-spacing:.01em}
    .ces-cta-rail__gift > span:last-child{min-width:0}
    /* An icon standing inside the sentence sits on the text's own baseline
       rather than being a flex item of the row. */
    .ces-cta-rail__gift-icon--inline{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-.25em;margin:0 .1rem}
    /* Centre the text block itself, so a wrapped second line stays under the
       first rather than ranging left inside a full-width span. */
    .ces-cta-rail__gift > span:last-child{text-align:center}
    .ces-cta-rail__gift-icon{display:inline-flex;width:1.6rem;height:1.6rem;flex:0 0 auto}
    .ces-cta-rail__gift-icon svg{width:100%;height:100%}
    .ces-cta-rail__main{display:inline-flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;
      justify-content:center;max-width:100%;gap:.2rem 1rem}
    /* display:flex here as well as the column: a rail that is not full-width
       never got the flex rule, so the two lines ran together on one. */
    .ces-cta-rail--gift .ces-button{display:flex;flex-direction:column;
      align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:.4rem;min-width:0;max-width:100%;
      padding:1.1rem 1.6rem;line-height:1.2}
    .ces-cta-rail--gift.ces-cta-rail--full .ces-button{min-height:7.2rem}
    @media screen and (min-width:750px){
      .ces-cta-rail__gift{font-size:1.45rem}
      .ces-cta-rail__gift-icon{width:1.8rem;height:1.8rem}
      .ces-cta-rail--gift.ces-cta-rail--full .ces-button{min-height:8rem}
    }
    .ces-cta-rail__arrow{display:inline-flex;width:2rem;flex:0 0 auto}
    .ces-cta-rail__arrow svg{width:100%;height:auto}
    @media screen and (min-width:750px){
      .ces-cta-rail__arrow{width:2.6rem}
    }
    /* A full-width button belongs to the block above it rather than floating
       between two sections, so it sits closer than a free-standing one. */
    .ces-cta-rail--full{margin-top:1.2rem}
    @media screen and (min-width:750px){
      .ces-cta-rail--full{margin-top:1.6rem}
    }
    .ces-cta-rail__note{margin:1.2rem 0 0;font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.45;opacity:.8}
    /* The trust items sit on one line where they fit and wrap as a pair when
       they do not, rather than stacking one per line on a narrow phone. */
    .ces-cta-rail__trust{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
      gap:.8rem 2rem;margin:1.2rem 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none}
    .ces-cta-rail__trust-item{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;
      font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3}
    .ces-cta-rail__trust-icon{display:inline-flex;width:1.8rem;height:1.8rem;flex:0 0 auto}
    .ces-cta-rail__trust-icon svg{width:100%;height:100%}
    @media screen and (min-width:750px){
      .ces-cta-rail{margin-top:3.2rem}
      .ces-cta-rail__note{font-size:1.4rem}
      .ces-cta-rail__trust-item{font-size:1.5rem}
      .ces-cta-rail__trust-icon{width:2rem;height:2rem}
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign rail_align = align | default: 'center'
    assign rail_width = width | default: 'auto'
  -%}
  <div class="ces-cta-rail ces-cta-rail--{{ rail_align }}{% if rail_width == 'full' %} ces-cta-rail--full{% endif %}{% if rail_gift != blank %} ces-cta-rail--gift{% endif %}">
    <div class="ces-cta-rail__box">
      <a class="ces-button" href="{{ url | default: '#ces-bundle' }}">
        <span class="ces-cta-rail__main">
          <span>{{ label }}</span>
          {%- if arrow and rail_gift == blank -%}
            <span class="ces-cta-rail__arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 26 14" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M0 7h22M17 1.5 23.5 7 17 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
                      stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if rail_gift != blank -%}
          <span class="ces-cta-rail__gift">
            {%- if rail_gift_icon != 'none' -%}
              <span class="ces-cta-rail__gift-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                {% render 'ces-icon', icon: rail_gift_icon %}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <span>
              {%- for chunk in rail_gift_chunks -%}
                {%- if chunk contains ']' -%}
                  {%- assign rail_bits = chunk | split: ']' -%}
                  {%- assign rail_inline_icon = rail_bits[0] | strip -%}
                  <span class="ces-cta-rail__gift-icon ces-cta-rail__gift-icon--inline" aria-hidden="true">
                    {% render 'ces-icon', icon: rail_inline_icon %}
                  </span>
                  {{- rail_bits[1] -}}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{- chunk -}}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </span>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>

    {%- if footnote != blank -%}
      {%- if rail_structured -%}
        <ul class="ces-cta-rail__trust" role="list">
          {%- for row in rail_rows -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign parts = row | strip_newlines | strip | split: '|'
              assign trust_icon = parts[0] | strip
              assign trust_label = parts[1] | strip
              if trust_label == blank
                continue
              endif
            -%}
            <li class="ces-cta-rail__trust-item">
              <span class="ces-cta-rail__trust-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                {% render 'ces-icon', icon: trust_icon %}
              </span>
              <span>{{ trust_label }}</span>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="ces-cta-rail__note">{{ footnote }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
